# xlang Documentation Authority

- `docs/` describes how the system **works now**. Write and implement against that reality.
- When the user contradicts existing code, README, or older docs, **the user’s rules win**. Ignore past implementation and README unless the user did not cover that topic.
- Do **not** add “future of development” notes unless the user explicitly allows that topic. Exception already documented: package manager server/backend only (`docs/PUBLISHING.md`).
- Do **not** mention monorepos in docs or design discussion for this project.
- Package/toolchain docs are English. Keep them present-tense (“does / aborts”), not “will / should someday”.
- When coding to match the package system, iterate until behavior matches `docs/PACKAGE_MANAGER.md` and related docs — docs win over current code.
